WEBVTT

00:06:29.540 --> 00:06:31.870
that fit into certain athletic niches,

00:06:31.870 --> 00:06:34.175
a form of artificial selection took place,

00:06:34.175 --> 00:06:36.798
a self-sorting for bodies that fit certain sports,

00:06:36.798 --> 00:06:39.458
and athletes' bodies became
more different from one another.

00:06:39.458 --> 00:06:43.414
Today, rather than the same size
as the average elite high jumper,

00:06:43.414 --> 00:06:44.428
the average elite shot-putter

00:06:44.428 --> 00:06:46.079
is two and a half inches taller

00:06:46.079 --> 00:06:49.168
and 130 pounds heavier.

00:06:49.168 --> 00:06:51.087
And this happened throughout the sports world.

00:06:51.087 --> 00:06:53.752
In fact, if you plot on a height versus mass graph

00:06:53.752 --> 00:06:56.280
one data point for each of two dozen sports

00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:59.565
in the first half of the 20th century, it looks like this.

00:06:59.565 --> 00:07:01.050
There's some dispersal,